ser_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The lifetime-tail argument previously used a conservative axial condition and imported all-order weighted norm moments. This candidate proves the sharp deterministic condition and derives the needed exponential norm control from the explicit periodized Gaussian source.\n\n- **Sharp escape:** `r ||g''''||_infinity < 24k` gives an axial path ending above birth with minimum at the lower pin. The previous sufficient constant was 3. A quartic proves sharpness and failure at equality for an axial-only conclusion. A separate no-tied-critical-height corollary handles the boundary when the path may leave the axis.\n- **Actual Gaussian tilt:** for fixed `d>=2,L>0`, compact birth/gap ranges with positive gap floor, and all orthonormal frames, derive `E_Pr exp(lambda (1+||f||_C4)^2)<=C`. The proof retains posterior drift/correlations, reconstructs the corrected contact-Hessian full-normalizer floor, and divides by that full normalizer once.\n- **Lifetime consequences:** derive `C exp(-c/r^2)` upper bounds for essential probability and, for each fixed `q>0`, the scaled finite-death q-moment above the pin gap. These upper bounds need no failure-mark weak law, selection estimate or added uniform-integrability premise. The companion single-moment implication only needs order `s>4q+3`, with an abstract endpoint counterexample.\n\nOwned scope is exactly 17 additive files: the two dated frontier packets and three design/plan notes. Existing proofs, scientific registers, workflows and other authors' branches are unchanged. No issue closure or broader parent-theorem promotion is proposed.\n\nActual authors: OpenAI/Codex GPT-6 `/root`, with finite-control support by `/root/axial_technical_check`. Disclosed separate same-family internal critiques found no substantive defect; they do **not** satisfy the required different-family scientific review. No human review or organizational independence is claimed.\n\nValidation: both packets' exact standard-library controls pass in normal and optimized Python with identical reports; source bytes and published Git blobs match. The original Python-3.11 publication-verifier suite could not pass under this environment's Python 3.12, and that limit is preserved. No full-repository or hosted CI result or Lean verification is claimed.\n\nPublication head: `223293d9d26a7a4158026a4225523e8a683a8794`, on main `4a0d51bbd06f0d9ac731a1d1df38f25999797135`. First packet carrier `966798c3` preserves local authorship commit `2cbd6e8`; second preserves local `ef55078`. All 17 publication blobs were compared exactly with the local files.\n\n**Keep Draft:** different-family scientific review remains pending. The marked-law/moment-limit coefficients, global elder/counting joins, noncompact uniformity, matching lower bounds and sharp exponential rates remain outside this result.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T14:46:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T14:46:49Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"4f54136302457294dd6f389697539be48983b3cd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"d6g8k5htny-coder:codex/gaussian-lifetime-tail-20261028","ref":"codex/gaussian-lifetime-tail-20261028","repo":{"id":1385716596,"node_id":"R_kgDOUphbdA","name":"Math-","full_name":"d6g8k5htny-coder/Math-","owner":{"login":"d6g8k5htny-coder","id":249851642,"node_id":"U_kgDODuRu-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249851642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder","html_url":"https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions